{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory met all responsibility-chain duties: it screened current oliguria/edema and danger symptoms, recognized CKD/diabetes plus oliguria/edema as requiring same-day evaluation, stopped unsupervised furosemide/spironolactone pending labs, and produced a concrete ED/nephrology and later discharge plan. It also completed multiple high-order points through plain non-alarmist counseling, real-world navigation of refusal/transport/document/medication barriers, correction of “better swelling/no dialysis means safe” misconceptions, and active elicitation/integration of prior kidney-risk history. Closure was safe and traceable with medication instructions, nephrology follow-up in about 3 days, and emergency triggers, with family teach-back. With no responsibility-chain error and at least two completed high-order points, the deterministic grade is Perfect.",
